# Chapter 02 final cutover independent review

Scope: b8dfdd1 versus 3fb8516 in C:/projects/NEPL3-doc-canonical-conformance, feat/doc-canonical-foundation. No tracked edits. Result: no remaining source/adoption blocker found. This bounded review does not imply canonical check, broader CI, GitHub display or bootstrap archive completion.

Source and contract: directly compared Git original authored blob with current doc/spec/02-foundation.nepld bytes: exactly equal. Old candidate path is absent. The full source/authoring preflight remains .tmp/preflight02/review.md: original preamble, all normative clauses, 18 original code payloads plus promoted FactDelta [start,end), ten Sections and no link dependencies preserved. Eight aliases agree with that mapping; unchanged Source/Range, schema/kind and Origin graph headings omit duplicate aliases. Actual automatic-heading behavior is a separate display gate.

Registry appends exactly the fourteenth foundation page and leaves all earlier page registrations unchanged. Markdown output_limits are byte-independent JSON-equal to base. Only HTML work (500M to 600M), nodes (20M to 24M), allocation (1B to 1.25B) change; other limits, production and per-page behavior are untouched. The progress note accurately records separate fresh-operation increases and does not invent a NodeLimit failure. Spec16 permits selecting explicit host limits before a new operation; it forbids implicit retry/resuming a stopped budget or substituting Markdown limits.

Independently inspected retained failures and command records. Initial .tmp/generation02 HTML stopped AllocationLimit with allocation 999,999,997/1B, work 427,925,810, nodes 18,233,447 and output 384. Next .tmp/generation02-expanded HTML stopped WorkLimit with work 499,999,997/500M, allocation 1,032,057,020, nodes 19,497,622 and output 480. Each command exited 1 and its requested HTML output directory is absent. These are stop-time counters, not complete output costs; neither run is counted as successful generation. Node headroom was selected prospectively, not described as measured exhaustion.

Independently walked successful .tmp/{markdown,html}-chapter02-resolved-first/second. All 15 Markdown files and all 16 HTML files equal byte-for-byte between runs. Recomputed every comparison-record size/hash and every manifest payload hash from files. All fourteen tracked Markdown projections equal first-run bytes. Five prior pages change only their metadata header: architecture, Math, Math HTML, conformance and model invariants; every prior body is identical to base. Compared .tmp/html-chapter06-first directly: thirteen previous HTML pages plus CSS (14 files) remain exactly equal.

Successful command records all exit zero and identify current registry SHA-256 f2b123da1abd264d528edc55caecd69129f5fb11706d8af4fcaf04d449438bdd. Fixed generation source checkpoint e82157a differs from adopted b8dfdd1 only in the six generated Markdown files. Thus registry/source/aliases and implementation inputs did not change during the recorded generation.

Receipt initial output usage is zero and every reported resource is below its declared bound. Markdown BEFORE RECEIPT SERIALIZATION: work 899,611,366/1B; nodes 37,173,598/40M; allocation 2,343,147,094/2.5B; output 916,300/10M; depth 14/1000. HTML reported usage: work 515,272,664/600M; nodes 19,679,272/24M; allocation 1,080,339,874/1.25B; output 1,134,314/10M; depth 14/1000. Source usage 393,161/10M and diagnostics/events zero in both. The Markdown field excludes receipt serialization and must not be advertised as the final charged total. Remaining allowances are finite and do not guarantee the next page fits.

Independently ran cargo test --locked -p nepl3-tools --lib documentation::markdown::tests after adoption: 10 passed, zero failed/ignored, 77 filtered. This includes exact foundation/Math generic code values, rejection of accidental generic tags, and five unquoting mutations using the real parser. It confirms the reviewed regression fix accommodates new legitimate foundation Ruby without disabling generic protection. No full tools rerun or broader runtime acceptance is claimed. Git diff --check against base passed and worktree was clean at inspection.

Final diff is confined to source move, registry/aliases, generated chapter02 and five context headers, plus explicit budget-stop/restart progress documentation. Root-owned canonical/repository/clippy/full-projection checks, actual GitHub navigation, CI and archive review remain separate. This review supports continuing those final cutover gates, not declaring T16/T21, all Doc migration or runtime conformance complete.
